#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:1
msgid "Adding New Intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:3
msgid ""
"cuda-oxide has two intrinsic contribution paths. Most device intrinsics are "
"**catalog-generated**: contributors edit reviewed catalog inputs and let "
"`cuda-intrinsics-gen` produce the API, dialect, importer, lowering, target, "
"reference, and probe surfaces together. Operations with bespoke verification "
"or lowering that the catalog cannot express remain hand-written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:9
msgid ""
"Start with [Catalog-Generated Intrinsics](catalog-generated-intrinsics.md) "
"unless you have established that the existing catalog model cannot represent "
"the operation. This chapter documents the compiler stages and the hand-"
"written path, using generated intrinsics as concrete examples of the "
"representations that flow through those stages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:17
msgid "The Five-Stage Pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:19
msgid "Every GPU intrinsic follows the same path through the compiler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:21
msgid ""
"cuda-device          User writes:  thread::threadIdx_x()\n"
"    │\n"
"    ▼\n"
"mir-importer       Compiler sees the call, emits a `dialect-nvvm` op\n"
"    │\n"
"    ▼\n"
"dialect-nvvm       The op lives here as a verified IR node\n"
"    │\n"
"    ▼\n"
"mir-lower          Converts the `dialect-nvvm` op into an LLVM dialect op\n"
"    │\n"
"    ▼\n"
"llvm-export        Exports textual LLVM IR  →  llc turns it into PTX\n"
msgstr ""

