#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:48
msgid "Example 1: `threadIdx_x` (the Simple Case)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:50
msgid ""
"`threadIdx_x()` is the \"Hello, World\" of GPU intrinsics: zero arguments, "
"one `u32` result, maps directly to a single LLVM NVVM intrinsic. If you can "
"follow this example, you can add any simple intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:54
#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:278
msgid "Stage 1 -- Declare in `cuda-device`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:56
msgid "**File:** `crates/cuda-device/src/thread.rs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:58
msgid ""
"#[inline(never)]\n"
"pub fn threadIdx_x() -> u32 {\n"
"    unreachable!(\"threadIdx_x called outside CUDA kernel context\")\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:65
msgid "Two rules that might look odd until you understand the trick:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:67
msgid ""
"**`#[inline(never)]`** keeps the function visible as a distinct call in MIR. "
"If rustc inlined it, the compiler would see `unreachable!()` instead of a "
"call it can intercept. That would be... less than helpful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:71
msgid ""
"**The body is `unreachable!()`** because this function never actually runs. "
"The compiler replaces the entire call with a `dialect-nvvm` operation before "
"any GPU code executes. Think of the function as a placeholder -- a \"dear "
"compiler, please insert a GPU instruction here\" note."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:77
msgid ""
"Document what LLVM IR or PTX the intrinsic maps to in a comment above the "
"function. Future you (or future contributors) will thank present you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:81
#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:302
msgid "Stage 2 -- Define the `dialect-nvvm` Op"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:83
msgid ""
"**File:** one of the hand-written op modules in `crates/dialect-nvvm/src/ops/"
"` -- `asm.rs`, `atomic.rs`, `cluster.rs`, `debug.rs`, `grid.rs`, `memory."
"rs`, or `wgmma.rs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:88
msgid ""
"Two kinds of op live in `dialect-nvvm`, and only one of them is written by "
"hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:91
msgid ""
"Anything described by `intrinsics/catalog.json` is **generated** by `cuda-"
"intrinsics-gen` into `crates/dialect-nvvm/src/ops/generated/`, where every "
"file opens with `// @generated by cuda-intrinsics-gen ... DO NOT EDIT.` The "
"op used as the example just below is one of them: `tid.x` is a catalog "
"intrinsic and its op lives in `ops/generated/sreg.rs` today. Adding an op "
"there by hand is undone by the next generator run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:98
msgid ""
"For the contributor workflow that owns those generated files, including "
"overlays, the append-only ABI ledger, regeneration, evidence, and local CI "
"gates, see [Catalog-Generated Intrinsics](catalog-generated-intrinsics.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:102
msgid ""
"The modules named above are the hand-written ones -- ops with bespoke "
"verification or lowering that the catalog does not describe. The code in "
"this section shows the shape an op takes either way; write it yourself only "
"for that second kind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:108
msgid ""
"#[pliron_op(name = \"nvvm.read_ptx_sreg_tid_x\", dialect = \"nvvm\", "
"format)]\n"
"pub struct ReadPtxSregTidXOp;\n"
"\n"
"impl Verify for ReadPtxSregTidXOp {\n"
"    fn verify(&self, ctx: &Context) -> Result<(), Error> {\n"
"        let op = &*self.get_operation().deref(ctx);\n"
"        if op.get_num_operands() != 0 {\n"
"            return verify_err!(op.loc(), \"expected 0 operands\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        if op.get_num_results() != 1 {\n"
"            return verify_err!(op.loc(), \"expected 1 result\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        Ok(())\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:126
msgid "Then register it so pliron knows the op exists:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:128
msgid ""
"pub(super) fn register(ctx: &mut Context) {\n"
"    ReadPtxSregTidXOp::register(ctx, ReadPtxSregTidXOp::parser_fn);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:134
msgid ""
"The `Verify` trait catches structural bugs early. If something accidentally "
"creates this op with two operands, verification fails with a clear message "
"instead of producing garbage PTX three stages later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:138
#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:337
msgid "Stage 3 -- Recognize in `mir-importer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:140
#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:339
msgid ""
"**File:** the intrinsic's family module under `crates/mir-importer/src/"
"translator/terminator/intrinsics/generated/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:143
msgid ""
"When the translator processes MIR, every function call passes through "
"`try_dispatch_intrinsic()` in `terminator/mod.rs`. The callee's fully "
"qualified domain name (FQDN) comes from `CrateDef::name()` via "
"`extract_func_info()`, producing paths like `cuda_device::thread::"
"threadIdx_x`. For a catalog intrinsic like `tid.x`, "
"`try_dispatch_intrinsic()` defers to the generated dispatcher, whose match "
"arm checks the FQDN:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:151
msgid ""
"\"cuda_intrinsics::__cuda_oxide_intrinsic_abi_v1::i0001\"\n"
"| \"cuda_device::thread::threadIdx_x\"\n"
"| \"cuda_device::threadIdx_x\" => {\n"
"    require_arity(name, args.len(), 0, &loc)?;\n"
"    Ok(Some(helpers::emit_generated_nvvm_intrinsic(\n"
"        ctx,\n"
"        ReadPtxSregTidXOp::get_concrete_op_info(),\n"
"        \"v1:i0001\",\n"
"        destination, target, block_ptr, prev_op,\n"
"        value_map, block_map, loc,\n"
"    )?))\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:166
msgid ""
"The arm matches the full module path (`cuda_device::thread::threadIdx_x`), "
"the re-exported name (`cuda_device::threadIdx_x`), and a versioned ABI "
"alias, so the call is intercepted regardless of how the user imports the "
"function. The FQDN is used as-is for matching -- no `::` to `__` conversion "
"happens before the intrinsic check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:172
msgid ""
"The `emit_generated_nvvm_intrinsic()` helper works for *any* zero-argument, "
"single-result NVVM intrinsic. It creates the operation, tags it with its "
"catalog ABI marker, stores the result in the value map, and emits a branch "
"to the next basic block. You never write this arm yourself: once the "
"reviewed overlay, ABI, and evidence inputs resolve into `intrinsics/catalog."
"json`, `cuda-intrinsics-gen` emits it. Hand-written arms in `terminator/mod."
"rs` exist only for what the catalog cannot describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:180
#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:385
msgid "Stage 4 -- Lower to the LLVM dialect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:182
msgid ""
"**File:** the intrinsic's family module under `crates/mir-lower/src/convert/"
"generated_intrinsics/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:184
msgid ""
"The op implements the `MirToLlvmConversion` op interface. For a catalog "
"intrinsic the impl is generated alongside a shared converter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:187
msgid ""
"#[op_interface_impl]\n"
"impl MirToLlvmConversion for ReadPtxSregTidXOp {\n"
"    fn convert(\n"
"        &self,\n"
"        ctx: &mut Context,\n"
"        rewriter: &mut DialectConversionRewriter,\n"
"        _operands_info: &OperandsInfo,\n"
"    ) -> Result<()> {\n"
"        convert_zero_operand_scalar_direct(\n"
"            ctx,\n"
"            rewriter,\n"
"            self.get_operation(),\n"
"            32,\n"
"            \"llvm_nvvm_read_ptx_sreg_tid_x\",\n"
"        )\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:207
msgid "The shared converter emits the LLVM intrinsic call:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:209
msgid ""
"fn convert_zero_operand_scalar_direct(\n"
"    ctx: &mut Context,\n"
"    rewriter: &mut DialectConversionRewriter,\n"
"    op: Ptr<Operation>,\n"
"    width: u32,\n"
"    intrinsic_name: &str,\n"
") -> Result<()> {\n"
"    let result_ty = IntegerType::get(ctx, width, Signedness::Signless);\n"
"    let function_ty = llvm_types::FuncType::get(ctx, result_ty.into(), vec!"
"[], false);\n"
"    let call = call_intrinsic(ctx, rewriter, op, intrinsic_name, "
"function_ty, vec![])?;\n"
"    rewriter.replace_operation(ctx, op, call);\n"
"    Ok(())\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:225
msgid ""
"Hand-written conversions for non-catalog ops follow the same pattern from "
"`convert/interface_impls.rs`, delegating into the `convert/intrinsics/` "
"modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:230
msgid ""
"LLVM intrinsic names use dots (`llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x`), but pliron "
"identifiers cannot contain dots. Internally we use underscores "
"(`llvm_nvvm_read_ptx_sreg_tid_x`). The export stage converts them back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:235
msgid "Stage 5 -- Export (Nothing to Change)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:237
msgid "**File:** `crates/llvm-export/src/export/` (the export module)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:239
msgid "The `CallOp` exporter already handles the underscore-to-dot conversion:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:241
msgid ""
"let fixed_name = if name.starts_with(\"llvm_nvvm\") {\n"
"    name.replace('_', \".\")\n"
"} else {\n"
"    strip_device_prefix(&name)\n"
"};\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:249
msgid ""
"Since `threadIdx_x` is *not* convergent (it is a per-thread register read, "
"not a collective operation), there is nothing to add to "
"`is_convergent_intrinsic()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:253
#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:469
msgid "**Final output:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:255
msgid ""
"declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n"
"%v5 = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:260
#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:480
msgid "After `llc`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:262
msgid "mov.u32  %r1, %tid.x;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:266
msgid "Five stages, one PTX instruction. Not bad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:270
msgid "Example 2: `shuffle_xor` (the Complex Case)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:272
msgid ""
"Warp shuffles are more interesting. The user's shorthand passes two "
"arguments, but the underlying LLVM intrinsic expects *four*. One extra (the "
"member mask) is filled in at the source level, the other (the clamp) by the "
"lowering. The operation is also **convergent**, meaning LLVM must not move, "
"duplicate, or speculate it across control flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:280
msgid "**File:** `crates/cuda-device/src/warp.rs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:282
msgid ""
"#[inline(never)]\n"
"pub fn shuffle_xor_sync(mask: u32, var: u32, lane_mask: u32) -> u32 {\n"
"    let _ = (mask, var, lane_mask);\n"
"    unreachable!(\"shuffle_xor_sync called outside CUDA kernel context\")\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"#[inline(always)]\n"
"pub fn shuffle_xor(var: u32, lane_mask: u32) -> u32 {\n"
"    shuffle_xor_sync(u32::MAX, var, lane_mask)\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:295
msgid ""
"The intrinsic stub is the masked `_sync` form, same pattern as before; the "
"`let _ = (mask, var, lane_mask);` suppresses unused-variable warnings -- a "
"small courtesy that costs nothing. The bare `shuffle_xor` shorthand is not a "
"stub at all: it is an `#[inline(always)]` wrapper that supplies the full-"
"warp mask (`u32::MAX`) and calls the stub. Only the `_sync` name is ever "
"matched by the compiler; the wrapper is ordinary Rust code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:304
msgid ""
"**File:** `crates/dialect-nvvm/src/ops/generated/warp_shuffle.rs`. The warp "
"shuffles are catalog intrinsics like `tid.x`, so this op is generated rather "
"than typed out; here is the real definition, condensed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:308
msgid ""
"/// Exchange a 32-bit value with a named XOR partner lane.\n"
"///\n"
"/// Operands are `[member_mask, value, lane_or_delta]`.\n"
"/// Generated lowering inserts the fixed clamp required by the selected "
"shuffle mode.\n"
"#[pliron_op(\n"
"    name = \"nvvm.shfl_sync_bfly_i32\",\n"
"    format,\n"
"    interfaces = [NOpdsInterface<3>, NResultsInterface<1>],\n"
")]\n"
"pub struct ShflSyncBflyI32Op;\n"
"\n"
"impl Verify for ShflSyncBflyI32Op {\n"
"    fn verify(&self, ctx: &Context) -> Result<(), Error> {\n"
"        let op = self.get_operation().deref(ctx);\n"
"        if op.get_num_operands() != 3 || op.get_num_results() != 1 {\n"
"            return verify_err!(\n"
"                op.loc(),\n"
"                \"nvvm.shfl_sync_bfly_i32 requires exactly [member_mask, "
"value, lane_or_delta] and one result\"\n"
"            );\n"
"        }\n"
"        // ... i32 type checks on all three operands and the result ...\n"
"        Ok(())\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:335
msgid ""
"Three operands this time (member mask, value, and lane mask), one result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:343
msgid ""
"The warp shuffles are catalog intrinsics, so their dispatch arms *and* their "
"argument-translating emitters are generated into `generated/warp_shuffle."
"rs`, next to the ops from Stage 2. Nothing about a shuffle is written by "
"hand. Hand-written dispatch lives in `try_dispatch_intrinsic()` in "
"`terminator/mod.rs` and covers what the catalog cannot describe. For "
"example, `core::intrinsics::typed_swap_nonoverlapping` (the primitive behind "
"`core::mem::swap`) is matched there and lowered by the hand-written "
"`emit_typed_swap()` in the same file as a load/load/store/store crossover "
"over two non-overlapping pointers. No catalog entry could say that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:354
msgid ""
"An intrinsic with arguments translates each of the user's operands before "
"building the op. Here is the generated arm for `shuffle_xor_sync`, condensed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:357
msgid ""
"\"cuda_device::warp::shuffle_xor_sync\" => {\n"
"    require_arity(name, args.len(), 3, &loc)?;\n"
"    let (member_mask, last_op) =\n"
"        rvalue::translate_operand(ctx, body, &args[0], /* ... */)?;\n"
"    let (value, last_op) =\n"
"        rvalue::translate_operand(ctx, body, &args[1], /* ... */)?;\n"
"    let (lane_or_delta, last_op) =\n"
"        rvalue::translate_operand(ctx, body, &args[2], /* ... */)?;\n"
"    let shuffle = ShflSyncBflyI32Op::build(ctx, member_mask, value, "
"lane_or_delta);\n"
"    helpers::set_generated_intrinsic_marker(ctx, shuffle, \"v1:i0051\");\n"
"    helpers::insert_op(ctx, shuffle, block_ptr, last_op);\n"
"    let result = shuffle.deref(ctx).get_result(0);\n"
"    Ok(Some(helpers::emit_store_result_and_goto(\n"
"        ctx, destination, result, target, /* ... */\n"
"        \"shuffle_xor_sync call without target block\",\n"
"    )?))\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:377
msgid ""
"The arm translates the user's MIR operands into pliron values -- typically "
"the results of `mir.load`s from each operand's alloca slot, or `mir."
"constant`s for literal arguments -- and wires them into the NVVM operation. "
"(These are not SSA values yet; `pliron::opts::mem2reg` will collapse the "
"load/store chains once translation is complete.) For a catalog intrinsic you "
"never write any of this: `cuda-intrinsics-gen` derives it from the resolved "
"generated catalog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:387
msgid "**File:** `crates/mir-lower/src/convert/intrinsics/warp.rs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:389
msgid ""
"Here is where the fourth argument appears. The `dialect-nvvm` op carries "
"three operands; the LLVM intrinsic for butterfly shuffle takes **four**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:392
msgid ""
"User's shorthand: shuffle_xor(value, lane_mask)                     →  2 "
"args\n"
"Intrinsic stub:   shuffle_xor_sync(mask, value, lane_mask)          →  3 "
"args\n"
"                                   ^^^^\n"
"                                   u32::MAX from the Stage 1 wrapper\n"
"LLVM intrinsic:   shfl.sync.bfly.i32(mask, value, lane_mask, clamp) →  4 "
"args\n"
"                                                             ^^^^^\n"
"                                                             always 31\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:402
msgid ""
"The converter forwards the three operands and adds only the clamp constant:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:404
msgid ""
"pub(crate) fn convert_shuffle_i32(\n"
"    ctx: &mut Context,\n"
"    rewriter: &mut DialectConversionRewriter,\n"
"    op: Ptr<Operation>,\n"
"    _operands_info: &OperandsInfo,\n"
"    intrinsic_name: &str,\n"
"    clamp: i32,\n"
") -> Result<()> {\n"
"    let i32_ty = IntegerType::get(ctx, 32, Signedness::Signless);\n"
"\n"
"    let operands: Vec<_> = op.deref(ctx).operands().collect();\n"
"    if operands.len() != 3 {\n"
"        return pliron::input_err_noloc!(\n"
"            \"Warp shuffle i32 requires 3 operands [mask, value, "
"lane_or_delta]\"\n"
"        );\n"
"    }\n"
"    let (mask, val, lane_or_delta) = (operands[0], operands[1], "
"operands[2]);\n"
"\n"
"    let clamp_val = create_i32_const(ctx, rewriter, clamp);\n"
"\n"
"    let func_ty = llvm_types::FuncType::get(\n"
"        ctx,\n"
"        i32_ty.into(),\n"
"        vec![i32_ty.into(), i32_ty.into(), i32_ty.into(), i32_ty.into()],\n"
"        false,\n"
"    );\n"
"\n"
"    let call_op = call_intrinsic(\n"
"        ctx, rewriter, op, intrinsic_name, func_ty,\n"
"        vec![mask, val, lane_or_delta, clamp_val],\n"
"    )?;\n"
"    rewriter.replace_operation(ctx, op, call_op);\n"
"    Ok(())\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:441
msgid ""
"The mask is an ordinary operand here, not a converter-made constant: the "
"Stage 1 wrapper baked in `u32::MAX` (all 32 lanes participate), and the "
"masked `_sync` forms let the user pass any mask at all. The clamp value of "
"`31`, supplied per shuffle mode by the generated `MirToLlvmConversion` impl "
"that calls this converter, means the shuffle spans the full warp width. It "
"is a fixed property of the instruction mode, and exposing it to the user "
"would just be noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:449
msgid "Stage 5 -- Export (Add Convergent)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:451
msgid ""
"Warp shuffles are **convergent** -- LLVM must not reorder them relative to "
"control flow. The export step checks `is_convergent_intrinsic()`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:454
msgid ""
"fn is_convergent_intrinsic(name: &str) -> bool {\n"
"    name == \"llvm.nvvm.barrier0\"\n"
"        || name.starts_with(\"llvm.nvvm.shfl\")      // shuffles\n"
"        || name.starts_with(\"llvm.nvvm.vote\")       // votes\n"
"        || name.starts_with(\"llvm.nvvm.mbarrier\")   // async barriers\n"
"        || name.starts_with(\"llvm.nvvm.cp.async.bulk\")\n"
"        // ...\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:465
msgid ""
"If your new intrinsic is convergent, add it here. If you forget, LLVM might "
"hoist it out of an `if` block, and your warp-level code will produce wrong "
"results or deadlock. Not great."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:471
msgid ""
"declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.shfl.sync.bfly.i32(i32, i32, i32, i32)\n"
"\n"
"%v8 = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.shfl.sync.bfly.i32(\n"
"    i32 -1, i32 %v3, i32 %v4, i32 31) #0\n"
"\n"
"attributes #0 = { convergent }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:482
msgid "shfl.sync.bfly.b32  %r3, %r1, %r2, 31;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:488
msgid "The Inline PTX Path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:490
msgid ""
"Some operations do not have LLVM intrinsics. For those, we emit inline PTX "
"assembly directly. The helper `inline_asm_convergent()` handles the "
"boilerplate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:493
msgid ""
"// wgmma fence: no inputs, no outputs, just a side effect\n"
"inline_asm_convergent(\n"
"    ctx, void_ty.into(), vec![],\n"
"    \"wgmma.fence.sync.aligned;\", \"\"\n"
");\n"
"\n"
"// mbarrier arrive: one input (pointer), one output (token)\n"
"inline_asm_convergent(\n"
"    ctx, i64_ty.into(), vec![ptr_val],\n"
"    \"mbarrier.arrive.shared.b64 $0, [$1];\", \"=l,r\"\n"
");\n"
msgstr ""

