#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:522
msgid "End-to-End: The Full Journey"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:524
msgid ""
"Here is every representation `threadIdx_x` passes through, top to bottom:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:526
msgid ""
"Rust:         thread::threadIdx_x()\n"
"MIR:          _3 = threadIdx_x() -> bb1\n"
"Pliron MIR:   %v = nvvm.read_ptx_sreg_tid_x : i32\n"
"Pliron LLVM:  %v = call i32 @llvm_nvvm_read_ptx_sreg_tid_x()\n"
"LLVM IR:      %v5 = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n"
"PTX:          mov.u32 %r1, %tid.x;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:535
msgid "And `shuffle_xor_sync`, the stub behind the `shuffle_xor` shorthand:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:537
msgid ""
"Rust:         warp::shuffle_xor_sync(u32::MAX, val, lane)\n"
"MIR:          _5 = shuffle_xor_sync(const u32::MAX, _3, _4) -> bb2\n"
"Pliron MIR:   %v = nvvm.shfl_sync_bfly_i32 %mask, %val, %lane : u32\n"
"Pliron LLVM:  %v = call i32 @llvm_nvvm_shfl_sync_bfly_i32(i32 -1, %val, "
"%lane, i32 31)\n"
"LLVM IR:      %v8 = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.shfl.sync.bfly.i32(i32 -1, %v3, %v4, "
"i32 31) #0\n"
"PTX:          shfl.sync.bfly.b32 %r3, %r1, %r2, 31;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:546
msgid ""
"Six representations. One Rust function call becomes one PTX instruction. The "
"intermediate steps exist so that each transformation is small, verifiable, "
"and independently testable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:552
msgid "Quick-Reference Checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:554
msgid ""
"For a hand-written intrinsic (one `intrinsics/catalog.json` cannot "
"describe), every file you need to touch, in order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:557
msgid ""
"**`cuda-device/src/<module>.rs`** -- `pub fn` with `#[inline(never)]` and "
"`unreachable!()` body. This is the user-facing API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:560
msgid ""
"**`dialect-nvvm/src/ops/<module>.rs`** -- `#[pliron_op(name = \"nvvm."
"<name>\", ...)]` struct, `Verify` impl (check operand/result counts), "
"`register()` call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:563
msgid ""
"**`mir-importer/src/translator/terminator/mod.rs`** -- `match` arm in "
"`try_dispatch_intrinsic()`, modelled on the hand-written `typed_swap` arm. "
"Zero-operand intrinsics are catalog territory: the generated dispatcher "
"emits them through `helpers::emit_generated_nvvm_intrinsic()`, which also "
"stamps the ABI marker a hand-written arm would have to stamp itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:569
msgid ""
"**`mir-lower/src/convert/interface_impls.rs`** -- `MirToLlvmConversion` impl "
"for the new op, dispatching to the converter function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:572
msgid ""
"**`mir-lower/src/convert/intrinsics/<module>.rs`** -- conversion logic. Use "
"`call_intrinsic()` for LLVM intrinsics, or `inline_asm_convergent()` for "
"inline PTX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:576
msgid ""
"**`llvm-export/src/export/`** -- *only if convergent*: add to "
"`is_convergent_intrinsic()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/adding-new-intrinsics.md:579
msgid ""
"For a catalog intrinsic, steps 2 through 4 are not yours to write. Extend "
"the appropriate `intrinsics/overlay/*.toml` family, append the ABI entry in "
"`intrinsics/abi-v1.toml`, add evidence only when the route requires it, and "
"regenerate. `intrinsics/catalog.json` is generated and must not be edited by "
"hand. See [Catalog-Generated Intrinsics](catalog-generated-intrinsics.md) "
"for the complete workflow."
msgstr ""

